# tools/c/control_in_population_witness.rish -- a guard whose population holds its own control has
# a failure mode that no care inside the guard prevents.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. A control proves a refusal by CONTAINING the thing refused. A scan proves a tree
# clean by reading a population. Where the population includes the control, those two
# correctnesses pull against each other, and the pull is invisible from inside either file: each
# is doing exactly its job. The defect lives in the PAIR.
#
# FOUND BY DOING, 20260916. `tools/fixtures/a/awk_lcg_exact_scan.sh` reads every tracked `.sh` and
# `.rish` source for an awk generator whose arithmetic leaves the range a double holds exactly,
# and gates the fed-back class at zero. Staging its own control took the live reading from
# `overflowing=0 exact=7 unread=17` to `5 / 8 / 18` and reddened that gate -- on five generators
# existing only to be refused inside a pen. The author had solved the same class one step over,
# reading past a `#` line so the scan's own header would not count itself, and nobody had asked
# the question of the control, whose plants are code rather than prose.
#
# THE QUESTION THIS RUNG ANSWERS is the one that lap booked twice and could not answer: how many
# other guards in this tree read a population that holds their own control?
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED, on metal. For every tracked `*_scan.sh`, the scan's OWN `git ls-files`
# invocation is read out of its source, RUN, and tested for whether any tracked file sharing the
# scan's basename stem stands inside the population that comes back.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED AND NEVER GATED, and the reason is the repair itself. Reading your own family
# is frequently correct: `awk_lcg_exact` deliberately does so today, with its numerals moved into
# shell variables and its plant heredocs unquoted, so the pen still receives literal arithmetic
# while the tracked bytes carry no refusable shape. A gate here would refuse the repaired shape
# and the unrepaired one in the same breath, and a gate that reds on a correct tree is a gate
# somebody turns off.
#
# TWO SEATED DOORS, and this rung names both rather than preferring one. `%775` ruled MOVE THE
# PLANT -- keep the population whole and take the refusable shape out of the tracked bytes, which
# is right where the exclusion would blind the next control to the same lesson.
# `tools/e/empty_document_witness.rish` rules READ PAST THE FIXTURES -- instrument is never field,
# which is right where the plant cannot leave without ceasing to be a plant. Which door fits is a
# judgment about the particular guard, and the census is what tells a reader there is a door to
# choose at all.
#
# THE DENOMINATOR IS SPLIT FOUR WAYS, because a first draft of this scan reported one
# `enumeration_unread` total and, inside it, silently dropped every bare `git ls-files` -- the
# whole tracked tree, the broadest population a scan can read and the likeliest to hold a control.
# `enumerating` is measured, `membership_test` is structurally outside the reading, and
# `enumeration_refused` and `no_git_population` are the two honest blind spots, each counted so a
# zero above is read as a zero of the measured denominator alone.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN, in both directions, because neither is fixable from here.
#   Upper, on enumeration: a scan may enumerate broadly and filter with a `case` pattern, so
#   membership in the enumeration is not proof the scan READS the file. The exact question is
#   whether a scan's numbers CHANGE when its control leaves the index, which wants a worktree per
#   candidate. The paper carries that reading and its cost.
#   Lower, on family: the pairing is by basename stem, which is a NAMING CONVENTION. The water
#   row's cardinal seat teaches that a measurement finding evidence by name reports the convention
#   it was handed, and this tree names some controls for the FAMILY rather than for the tool. The
#   true count is at or above the one printed.
#
# THIS FAMILY IS A MEMBER OF ITS OWN CLASS, which is the finding proving itself. The scan reads
# every tracked `*_scan.sh` with a bare `git ls-files`, so its own control stands inside its own
# population, and `--explain` on the scan names it. That costs nothing here for two reasons worth
# saying plainly: the scan reports rather than gating, and every plant this family writes lives in
# a pen repository at run time rather than in the tracked bytes -- `%775`'s ruling, applied by the
# instrument that measures the ruling's own subject. Leg `plant_not_tracked` holds it there.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/c/control_in_population_witness.rish

say "control-in-population: Language EN -- a control proves a refusal by holding what the scan refuses."
say "control-in-population: Style Gauge at Field -- every figure carries its denominator and both blind spots."
say "control-in-population: Lens TAME -- safety first: a defect living in a pair is invisible from inside either half."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/control_in_population_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "control-in-population: the census must complete before it is believed"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=reported" else "control-in-population: this reading reports and never gates"
assert scan.out contains "family_pairing=basename_stem" else "control-in-population: the naming convention the count depends on must be said out loud"
assert scan.out contains "enumeration_refused=" else "control-in-population: the unmeasured half must be counted rather than assumed empty"
assert scan.out contains "no_git_population=" else "control-in-population: a scan reading no tracked population is counted apart, never proven clear"
assert scan.out contains "membership_test=" else "control-in-population: a predicate over one path is not a population and earns its own class"
say "census GREEN -- the class is counted, and both blind spots are named rather than guessed at"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/control_in_population_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "control-in-population: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "control-in-population: the control must agree with itself"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "control-in-population: every leg must stand, and a leg written tomorrow must be heard today"
assert control.out contains "bare_ls_files_enumerates=yes" else "control-in-population: a bare git ls-files is the whole tracked tree and must never be dropped"
assert control.out contains "bare_ls_files_self_reads=yes" else "control-in-population: the broadest population must be read for its own family"
assert control.out contains "bare_ls_files_names_control=yes" else "control-in-population: the control subset must be told apart from the family reading"
assert control.out contains "narrow_enumerates=yes" else "control-in-population: a narrow population is measured, never skipped"
assert control.out contains "narrow_self_reads_zero=yes" else "control-in-population: a population that cannot reach its own family must read zero"
assert control.out contains "narrow_control_zero=yes" else "control-in-population: the clear direction is asserted as hard as the refusal"
assert control.out contains "membership_test_counted=yes" else "control-in-population: an error-unmatch predicate belongs in its own class"
assert control.out contains "membership_not_enumerating=yes" else "control-in-population: a predicate must never be counted as a population"
assert control.out contains "variable_glob_refused=yes" else "control-in-population: a glob held in a shell variable is unmeasured and must say so"
assert control.out contains "find_only_counted=yes" else "control-in-population: a scan naming no git ls-files is counted apart rather than vanishing"
assert control.out contains "find_only_not_enumerating=yes" else "control-in-population: a find-rooted population is not this instrument's measured class"
assert control.out contains "prose_is_not_invocation=yes" else "control-in-population: a header teaching the command must not be read as a call"
assert control.out contains "family_self_reads=yes" else "control-in-population: a witness of the same family counts as self-reading"
assert control.out contains "family_control_flag_off=yes" else "control-in-population: the two readings answer different questions and must move apart"
assert control.out contains "explain_names_control=yes" else "control-in-population: explain must name the family file, so the judgment is one command away"
assert control.out contains "list_prints_one_row=yes" else "control-in-population: list must print one row per hit"
assert control.out contains "plant_not_tracked=yes" else "control-in-population: this family's own plants live in a pen, never in the tracked bytes"
assert control.out contains "reports_never_refuses=yes" else "control-in-population: the census must never refuse a tree"
assert control.out contains "verdict_is_reported=yes" else "control-in-population: the verdict must say plainly that it reports"

say "control-in-population GREEN -- 19 legs on real git repositories in a throwaway pen"
say "control-in-population: the census is itself a member of the class it counts, and its own plants live in the pen"
